# Breadcrumbs

Show breadcrumbs only when they reflect a real parent route. They are navigation for people who arrive deep in the documentation, not a record of where they have been and not a measure of progress through a task.

**Reference pattern.** The examples document a local adaptation. They do not add a publishing backend or a new Home Assistant capability.

## Use the shared hierarchy contract

[Breadcrumbs](../../components/breadcrumbs.html#usage) owns parent routes, the navigation landmark and current-page semantics. This page keeps the publishing context and both examples. Choose the parent-only or current-item variant deliberately. Both must describe the same hierarchy.

## When to use it

Use a short trail when someone can land directly on a device guide or a nested help page, for example Help, then Cameras. Link the real parent area. A dashboard already oriented by its sidebar and room title may not need another trail.

## Structure and behaviour

Use a named navigation landmark and an ordered list. Keep each parent label the same as its destination title. Show the current page as plain text or with aria-current="page". Decorative separators must not be read out as content. The site shell owns the primary breadcrumb implementation.

## Home Assistant boundary

A breadcrumb does not describe browser history. Do not build a parent route from a dashboard URL, assume every entity belongs to one room, or copy a government topic taxonomy into Home Assistant.

